menu "Example Configuration"

    config ENABLE_ALIRO_BLE_UWB
        bool "Enable Aliro (Apple Home Key) over BLE + UWB"
        default y
        help
            Advertise the Door Lock cluster's Aliro Provisioning + BLE-UWB
            features and register the Aliro reader delegate, so Apple Home can
            provision an Express (BLE + UWB) Home Key into Wallet for this reader.

    config ENABLE_HA_MQTT
        bool "Publish distance and access events to Home Assistant over MQTT"
        default n
        depends on ENABLE_ALIRO_BLE_UWB
        select WOZ_ALIRO_ACCESS_LISTENER
        help
            Publish UWB distance and Aliro access verdicts straight to a TLS
            MQTT broker, on the topics MQTT Discovery expects, so Home
            Assistant builds the device
            through MQTT Discovery with no host-side agent running. Lock
            control stays on Matter; this carries only what Matter does not
            expose.

            Off by default: it adds esp-mqtt and a TLS session to the image,
            and it is useless until a broker is provisioned. Nothing about a
            broker is compiled in — host, port, login, CA certificate and node
            name are runtime NVS config, set with the `hamqtt` console command.

            Do not set this on its own. Build with `make build HAMQTT=1`, which
            also applies the mbedTLS record sizing in
            sdkconfig.defaults.hamqtt; without it mbedtls_ssl_setup cannot get
            a contiguous 16 KiB input record next to Matter, NimBLE and Wi-Fi,
            and every connection fails with -0x7F00 before the handshake.

endmenu
